Bill Doss wrote:
> mean is that I'd rather have two spells that I can cast successfully,
> i.e. 0% failure rate, than one at 0% and another at near 100% failure.
>  I accept that would mean I would start with two low level spells.

I don't think it's possible to start with a spell with 100% failure
(well, maybe if you have really bad stats)

> Regarding magic missile, I love magic missile.  When my wizard is
> lucky enough to start with it, he can always use it right away.

No, he can't, not without a potion of gain energy or newt corpses.

> So
> why then are some of these harder spells "castable" right away while
> some are not?

Attack spells are easier to cast because you start with basic skills in
the attack spell school. If you get a spell from a different spell
school, you have to train it to basic before you get acceptable spell
failure.

> I still say give me two spells that I can cast successfully right
> away, regardless of their level, rather than one I can use and one I
> can't.

You can't use magic missile right away, because you won't have enough PW
at the beginning (the same applies to all 2nd level spells, I guess).
And once you have enough PW and basic skills in the appropriate spell
school you can cast every starting spell with 0% failure (I guess).

